\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-partial\fR
Send partial=true instead of partial=false, which Emporix treats alike.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx fees create"
Create a fee.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx fees create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the fee in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object with code (unique in the tenant), name, feeType (PERCENT, ABSOLUTE or ABSOLUTE_MULTIPLY_ITEMQUANTITY), feePercentage or feeAbsolute (amount and currency), siteCode and active, and optionally itemType (PRODUCT or PAYMENTTYPE), taxable with taxCode, and activeTimespan, e.g. \fB{"code": "deposit", "name": {"en": "Deposit"}, "feeType": "ABSOLUTE", "feeAbsolute": {"amount": 0.25, "currency": "EUR"}, "siteCode": "AcmeStore_NL", "active": true}\fR. Without an id, Emporix makes one; the response gives it and its YRN. A code that the tenant has already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. The Fee Service ignores Content\-Language: it stores a string as sent, in no language, in place of any translations.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the fee.fee_create scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx fees delete"
Delete a fee.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx fees delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the fee ID, which no item has then. Emporix answers an unknown ID as one that it deleted (204 No Content).
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the fee.fee_delete scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx fees for\-item"
List the fees of an item on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx fees for\-item YRN [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads fees, surcharges on items such as products or payment types. Emporix filters fees by site and documents main as the default site, so list, for\-product and for\-item require \fB\-\-site\fR; an unknown site lists nothing. TYPE is PERCENT, ABSOLUTE or ABSOLUTE_MULTIPLY_ITEMQUANTITY (the amount times the item quantity), AMOUNT the percentage or the amount in its currency, ITEM TYPE the type of item the fee applies to (PRODUCT or PAYMENTTYPE), and FROM and TO the active time span. YRN names the item, e.g. \fB\(aqurn:yaas:saasag:caasproduct:product:TENANT;PRODUCT_ID\(aq\fR (quoted, because the shell would end the command at ;). An unknown item lists nothing; Emporix fails on a malformed YRN.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, CODE, NAME, TYPE, AMOUNT, ITEM TYPE, SITE, ACTIVE, TAXABLE, FROM, TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx fees for\-product"
List the fees of a product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx fees for\-product PRODUCT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads fees, surcharges on items such as products or payment types. Emporix filters fees by site and documents main as the default site, so list, for\-product and for\-item require \fB\-\-site\fR; an unknown site lists nothing. TYPE is PERCENT, ABSOLUTE or ABSOLUTE_MULTIPLY_ITEMQUANTITY (the amount times the item quantity), AMOUNT the percentage or the amount in its currency, ITEM TYPE the type of item the fee applies to (PRODUCT or PAYMENTTYPE), and FROM and TO the active time span. PRODUCT_ID is the product id (as in \fBepx products list\fR), not its code. An unknown id lists nothing.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, CODE, NAME, TYPE, AMOUNT, ITEM TYPE, SITE, ACTIVE, TAXABLE, FROM, TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
