.SS "epx fees update"
Replace or change a fee.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx fees update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the fee ID with the one in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object as create takes it, or with \fB\-\-partial\fR changes only the members that it gives, which still include code, siteCode, active and feeType (Emporix refuses the body otherwise). Emporix answers an unknown ID with 409 Conflict (exit 5), not as not found.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. The Fee Service ignores Content\-Language: it stores a string as sent, in no language, in place of any translations.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the fee.fee_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-partial\fR
Change only the fields that the body gives; without it, the body replaces the whole fee.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
